.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PCOMPRESS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pcompress
.Nd parallel, deduplicating, multi-algorithm compressor and archiver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c Ar algorithm
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Op Fl t Ar threads
.Op Fl S Ar checksum
.Op Fl DEFGLPx
.Op Fl B Ar 0-5
.Op Fl e Ar cipher Op Fl w Ar pwfile Op Fl k Ar keylen
.Op Fl CM
.Ar file
.Op Ar target | Fl
.Nm
.Fl p
.Fl c Ar algorithm
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Fl a
.Op Fl c Ar algorithm
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Op Fl jnTvx
.Op Ar options
.Ar path ...
.Ar archive | Fl
.Nm
.Fl d
.Op Fl mK
.Op Fl w Ar pwfile
.Ar file | Fl
.Op Ar target
.Nm
.Fl i
.Ar archive
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
splits its input into chunks and compresses them in parallel, one chunk
per thread.
It can deduplicate data within a chunk or across the whole input, delta-encode
similar blocks, run content-aware filters, and encrypt and authenticate
every chunk.
With
.Fl a
it archives files and directories into a PAX stream and compresses that.
Each chunk carries a checksum of its original data, which is verified on
decompression.
.Pp
Output files get a
.Pa .pz
suffix unless the name already has one.
.Nm
refuses to overwrite an existing output file.
.Sh MODES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar algorithm
Compress a single
.Ar file
into
.Ar target ,
or into
.Ar file Ns Pa .pz
if no target is given.
If
.Ar target
is
.Fl ,
write to standard output.
.It Fl p
Pipe mode: read standard input, write standard output.
Requires
.Fl c .
.It Fl a
Archive mode.
Every
.Ar path
is archived; the last argument names the archive
.Pq or Fl No for standard output .
The default algorithm is
.Cm adapt2 .
Paths are stored as given on the command line, as with
.Xr tar 1 .
.It Fl d
Decompress
.Ar file
.Pq or standard input if Fl .
For a single-file stream,
.Ar target
names the output file; it defaults to the input name without
.Pa .pz ,
or with
.Pa .out
appended.
When the input is
.Fl
and no target is given, output goes to standard output.
For an archive,
.Ar target
is the directory to extract into, created if necessary; it defaults
to the current directory.
.It Fl i
List the members of an archive without extracting them.
.It Fl h
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l Ar level
Compression level, 1 (fastest) to 14 (smallest); default 6
.Pq 1 for Cm lz4 .
Unless advanced options are given, higher levels also turn on
features, see
.Sx LEVELS .
.It Fl s Ar size
Maximum chunk size; a number with an optional
.Cm k ,
.Cm m
or
.Cm g
suffix.
Default 8m, larger at levels above 8.
Minimum 2048 bytes, maximum 80% of physical memory.
Deduplication needs chunks of at least 1m
.Pq 2m for Fl G .
.It Fl t Ar threads
Number of worker threads, 1 to 256; default is the number of CPUs.
Each thread holds about two chunks in memory.
.It Fl S Ar checksum
Chunk verification checksum:
.Cm CRC64 , SHA256 , SHA512 , KECCAK256 , KECCAK512 , BLAKE256
.Pq default
or
.Cm BLAKE512 .
.Cm CRC64
cannot be used with deduplication.
.It Fl D
Deduplicate variable-sized blocks within each chunk, using Rabin
fingerprinting.
.It Fl F
Deduplicate fixed-size blocks.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl D
or
.Fl E .
.It Fl G
Deduplicate across the whole input using an in-memory index
.Pq with Fl D No by default, or Fl F .
When the index would not fit in memory, a segmented index is kept on
disk instead.
Not available in pipe mode, and a stream compressed with
.Fl G
must be decompressed to a file, not to standard output.
.It Fl E
Delta-encode blocks that are similar to an earlier block, using bsdiff;
implies
.Fl D .
Repeat
.Pq Fl EE
to accept less similar blocks.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl G .
.It Fl B Ar n
Average deduplication block size: 0 = 2KB, 1 = 4KB, ... 5 = 64KB.
.It Fl L
LZP pre-compression.
.It Fl P
Adaptive delta encoding of numeric tables.
.It Fl x
Dispack filter for 32-bit x86 Windows executables
.Pq archive mode only .
.It Fl j
PackJPG and PackPNM filters for JPEG and PNM images, and WavPack for
WAV audio if built in
.Pq archive mode only .
.It Fl T
Do not store archive metadata in a separate stream.
.It Fl n
Do not sort archive members by type before archiving.
.It Fl v
Verbose: list archive members as they are processed.
.It Fl m
On extraction restore all permissions, ACLs and extended attributes;
ownership is restored only when run as root.
.It Fl K
On extraction do not overwrite files that are newer than the archived
copy.
.It Fl e Ar cipher
Encrypt with
.Cm AES
or
.Cm SALSA20
in counter mode, keyed by scrypt from a password.
Every chunk and the header are authenticated with an HMAC.
A new key is derived for every run.
.It Fl w Ar pwfile
Read the password from
.Ar pwfile ,
which is overwritten with zeros afterwards.
Otherwise the password is prompted for on the terminal.
Required in pipe mode.
.It Fl k Ar keylen
Key length in bytes, 16 or 32; default 32.
.It Fl C
Print compression statistics.
.Fl CC
also prints the offset and length of every deduplication block.
.It Fl M
Accepted and ignored (memory allocator statistics were removed in 4.1).
.El
.Sh ALGORITHMS
.Bl -tag -width "adapt2" -compact
.It Cm lzfx
fast, average ratio
.It Cm lz4
very fast
.It Cm zlib
fast, good ratio
.It Cm zstd
fast with a very good ratio; multithreaded within a chunk
.It Cm bzip2
slow, better ratio than zlib
.It Cm lzma
very slow, very high ratio
.It Cm lzmaMt
multithreaded lzma
.It Cm ppmd
slow, best for text
.It Cm libbsc
block-sorting, fast with a high ratio
.It Cm adapt
per chunk: ppmd for text, bzip2 otherwise
.It Cm adapt2
per chunk: ppmd for text, lzma otherwise; best for archives
.It Cm none
no compression, for use with deduplication
.El
.Sh LEVELS
Without any of
.Fl DEFGLPjx ,
the level selects features:
.Bl -tag -width "11-14" -compact
.It 1-3
compression only
.It 4
global deduplication, 8KB blocks
.It 5-8
plus adaptive delta encoding
.It 9
plus dispack, larger chunks
.It 10
plus LZP and extra delta passes
.It 11-14
plus PackJPG/PackPNM/WavPack
.El
.Pp
Global deduplication is not enabled automatically when the output or
input is a pipe.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PCOMPRESS_INDEX_MEM
Memory limit for the global deduplication index, in megabytes.
.It Ev PCOMPRESS_CACHE_DIR
Directory for global deduplication temporary files; defaults to
.Ev TMPDIR
then
.Ev HOME .
.It Ev PCOMPRESS_CHUNK_HASH_GLOBAL
Block hash for global deduplication:
.Cm SHA256
.Pq default ,
.Cm SHA512 , KECCAK256 , KECCAK512 , BLAKE256 , BLAKE512 , SKEIN256
or
.Cm SKEIN512 .
.El
.Sh PASSWORDS
The whole password is used, up to 4096 bytes, whether typed or read from
.Fl w .
Releases up to 4.1.0 read at most 15 bytes of a password file longer than
16 bytes and refused typed passwords longer than 14; files they wrote still
decrypt with the same password file.
A file encrypted from a password longer than 16 bytes cannot be read by
4.1.0 or earlier.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Status 2 means a usage error.
A corrupt or truncated input, a failed checksum or HMAC, and any write
or extraction error are reported and make
.Nm
exit with status 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compress a file with zstd at level 9 and restore it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pcompress -c zstd -l9 data.tar
$ pcompress -d data.tar.pz data.tar.restored
.Ed
.Pp
Archive a directory with all features, then extract it elsewhere:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pcompress -a -l14 src/ src-backup
$ pcompress -d src-backup.pz /tmp/restore
.Ed
.Pp
Stream through a pipe with encryption:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ tar cf - dir | pcompress -p -c lz4 -e AES -w pw > dir.tar.pz
$ pcompress -d -w pw - < dir.tar.pz | tar xf -
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bzip2 1 ,
.Xr gzip 1 ,
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr xz 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1
.Pp
.Pa README.md
and
.Pa DESIGN.md
in the source distribution.
